    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the number of functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is equal to........"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "360",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>as</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Now taking cases we get,</p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mappings</mtext></math></p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mappings</mtext></math></p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mappings</mtext></math></p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mappings</mtext></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mapping&#160;each</mtext></math></p><p>So, total number of function will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn></math></p>"
